{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0136ZfkBDoJLWdAtg2i81mp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A few options, in order of how much you'd reach for them:\n\n1. **Master slide edit (View → Master Slide)** — change the font on the master's title/content placeholders. This only affects text that *inherits* from the master, so any text box added manually with overridden fonts won't update.\n\n2. **Tools → Macros (Basic)** — most reliable for \"every text box on every slide.\" A short macro iterates `ThisComponent.DrawPages` → each shape → each paragraph/portion and sets `CharFontName = \"Liberation Sans Narrow\"`. Want me to write it?\n\n3. **Edit the .odp directly** — .odp is a zip; unzip, run a sed/regex over `content.xml` and `styles.xml` to replace `fo:font-name`/`style:font-name-*` values, rezip. Fast and scriptable, but easy to corrupt the file if you're not careful — keep a backup.\n\nI'd recommend the macro: it's safe, runs against the open document, and handles inherited *and* overridden text. Say the word and I'll write it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9799,"cache_read_input_tokens":17712,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9799},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cbe7561c-43e7-4a8d-929b-7ca55462eafa","uuid":"500c366d-c14f-42e4-b9f2-efb099f740b3"}
